  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The list ranks government contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total obligations across the ranked universe are $237B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. leads the ranking with $19.9B in obligations. The list records contractors from health services and defense primes to construction and shipbuilding, including TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $14.5B, FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO at $13.4B, and multiple entries for LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $12.5B and $10.8B. The ranking mixes prime contractors and large services firms, reflecting obligations rather than contract counts or award values. All figures are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Use the ranking to identify where federal dollars have been obligated so far in FY2026, not to measure completed performance or full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who tops the FY2026 to date contractor ranking?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the top contractor by obligations, at $19.9B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP follows at $14.5B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is third at $13.4B. The list includes a mix of healthcare, defense, and construction firms."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the obligations list represent and how should you use it?",
        "body": "The list represents contract obligations for the fiscal year to date, totaling $237B across the ranked set. Use the list to track where obligations have been placed so far in FY2026; obligations are not the same as completed work or full-year awards. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Who is the largest federal contractor in FY2026?",
      "a": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the largest federal contractor in FY2026, with $19.9B in obligations. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. sits ahead of TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $14.5B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO at $13.4B."
    },
    {
      "q": "How are these contractor rankings calculated?",
      "a": "They are ranked by total contract obligations for the fiscal year to date. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
